Usage: killall [OPTION]... NAME...

Signal processes by executable name.
On Windows, TERM/KILL are mapped to Win32 termination.

OPTIONS:
  -e, --exact        require an exact process-name match
  -I, --ignore-case  match case insensitively
  -q, --quiet        do not complain if no processes were killed
  -v, --verbose      report successful signals
  -0                 only check for matching processes
  -9                 send SIGKILL; mapped to Win32 termination
  -TERM              send SIGTERM; mapped to Win32 termination
  -SIGTERM           send SIGTERM; mapped to Win32 termination
  -KILL              send SIGKILL; mapped to Win32 termination
  -SIGKILL           send SIGKILL; mapped to Win32 termination
      --help         display this help and exit
  -V, --version      output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
